weaknesses.value:
- While the paper discusses a pretraining phase and an in-context learning phase, it doesn't clearly address how the transition between these phases is managed or optimized. Also, the instruction-tuning phase might be missing to ensure the success of in-context learning and mixture of tasks as defined in the paper; 
- Some empirical valuations including flipping labels could also be valuable to add [1, 2]; 


[1] Min, Sewon, et al. "Metaicl: Learning to learn in context." arXiv preprint arXiv:2110.15943 (2021).

[2] Wei, Jerry, et al. "Symbol tuning improves in-context learning in language models." arXiv preprint arXiv:2305.08298 (2023).

